'''Mitsuya Kofun''' (三津屋古墳) is an {{ill|Octagonal Kofun|lt=Octagonal Kofun|ja|八角墳}} located in {{ill|Yoshioka, Gunma|ja|吉岡町}}, Gunma Prefecture. It is designated as a Gunma Prefectural Historic Site.
{{ill|Mitsuya Kofun|ja|三津屋古墳}} is a [[Kofun]] in Japan. Specifically, it is an {{ill|Octagonal Kofun|lt=Octagonal Kofun|ja|八角墳}}.<ref name=":0">{{Cite web |date=2015-09-07 |title=Mitsuya Kofun [三津屋古墳] Passage Grave : The Megalithic Portal and Megalith Map |url=https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=31732 |access-date=2023-10-20 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20150907095743/https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=31732 |archive-date=2015-09-07 }}</ref> A rare kind of tomb mostly reserved for 7th century [[Emperor of Japan|Emperors of Japan]].{{sfn|Niiro|1992|p=160}}<ref>{{Cite web |title=Gobyōyama Kofun (in Kyōto) |url=https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=33021 |access-date=2023-10-21}}</ref>[[Emperor Jomei|i]]<ref>{{Cite web |last=Hays |first=Jeffrey |title=ASUKA, FUJIWARA AND ASUKA-ERA CITIES AND TOMBS {{!}} Facts and Details |url=https://factsanddetails.com/japan/cat16/sub106/entry-5299.html#chapter-16 |access-date=2023-10-20 |website=factsanddetails.com |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":02">{{Cite web |date=2023-10-16 |title=Dan-no-tsuka Kofun [Dannotsuka Kofun 段ノ塚古墳, Jomei Tennō-ryō Jomei Tennnoryo 舒明天皇] Passage Grave : The Megalithic Portal and Megalith Map |url=https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=33044 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20231016234831/https://www.megalithic.co.uk/article.php?sid=33044 |archive-date=2023-10-16 |access-date=2023-10-20}}</ref>.<ref name=":1">{{Cite web |title=Kengoshizuka Kofun Tumulus, Koshitsuka-gomon Kofun Tumulus |url=http://asuka-japan-heritage.jp/global/en/saimei/detail/kengosiduka_sa.html |access-date=2023-10-20 |website=Exploring the Footsteps of the Heroines of Asuka |language=en}}</ref><ref name=":2">{{Cite news |date=2022-03-04 |title=Octagonal burial mound said to belong to ancient Japan empress reconstructed in Nara Pref. |language=en |work=Mainichi Daily News |url=https://mainichi.jp/english/articles/20220304/p2a/00m/0na/040000c |access-date=2023-10-20}}</ref>, The inner cha